#, rust-format
msgid ""
"1. Open your router's admin page (often the gateway address, such as "
"192.168.1.1).\n"
"2. Find Port Forwarding (sometimes called Virtual Servers or NAT).\n"
"3. Forward TCP port {} to this computer's local address.\n"
"4. Share the internet link, using your public address in place of the local "
"one.\n"
"5. Remove the forward when you are done."
msgstr ""
"1. Open your router's admin page (often the gateway address, such as "
"192.168.1.1).\n"
"2. Find Port Forwarding (sometimes called Virtual Servers or NAT).\n"
"3. Forward TCP port {} to this computer's local address.\n"
"4. Share the internet link, using your public address in place of the local "
"one.\n"
"5. Remove the forward when you are done."

